			<div class="content" id="post-content-2545002">
									

<p>I knew I was forgetting something, edited my first post to include thanks to the people who helped me.</p>
<p>As for Dr. Warm's contention, let me try to explain what my thinking was there. The sole reason for its inclusion was to show how incredibly difficult it is to test a thing whose anomalous property is that it can't be observed; I went into way more detail on this in my first draft before smarter people than me noted that it really made the article drag, so I cut most of that stuff out. I wasn't trying to go full on <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-055">SCP-055</a> (which does that whole thing better than I ever could) but I did at least want to hint at how tough it is to figure out creative ways to actually figure out the parameters of this anomaly.</p>
<p>Also, I had it in my mind that pretty much everyone at the Foundation immediately assumed it was memetic in nature and that Dr. Warm was just coming up with a fringe idea, which is why I used the word &quot;contention&quot; rather than &quot;theory&quot;. The point I was making was that it took 22 separate tests before they could actually conclusively disprove it despite it being a fairly goofy idea. That's how hard it was to test.</p>
<p>If all that doesn't make sense then I'll remove the line. If it makes sense but doesn't come across in the article then I'll figure out a way to rewrite it so it's clearer.</p>

