					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/scorpion451" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1918720); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1918720&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606360608" alt="Scorpion451" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1918720)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/scorpion451" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1918720); return false;" >Scorpion451</a></span> <span class="odate time_1469718696 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">28 Jul 2016 15:11</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2545149">
									

<p>I'm thinking it's a little bit of a Schrodinger's Box effect, and partly exploiting the fact that there are mechanical limits to the non-observation effect. It doesn't directly detect observe people- only the weight of the box-o-unknown-contents it's attached to- and it doesn't report that information to anything but it's own cutoff switch. Basically it works for the same reason that the guy got trampled- the other people are still there as far as the laws of physics are concerned, you just can't directly perceive them or their actions.</p>
<p>Personally, I'd want to hook up a readout to the sensor, and see whether:</p>
<ul>
<li>a) it would show you the actual weight of the elevator and contents<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-31215-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-31215-1')">1</a></sup></li>
<li>b) it ceased to detect the other people and let the over-capacity elevator try to work<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-31215-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-31215-2')">2</a></sup></li>
<li>or c) it showed you only your own weight but still functioned properly by not letting the elevator work when over capacity.</li>
</ul>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-31215-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-31215-1')">1</a>. which would still tell you nothing definitive about the presence of other people, only that this was an exceptionally heavy elevator and that it may or may not change its weight randomly when you aren't looking.</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-31215-2"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-31215-2')">2</a>. because each person saw only their own weight, and none of them triggered the sensor individually.</div>
</div>

